    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Here's a surprise: gravity is still there! Up at the space station, Earth is still pulling on them.",
      "punch": "gravity",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌍",
        "text": "Gravity is still there!",
        "cue": "gravity",
        "sub": "Earth is still pulling",
        "sub_cue": "pulling"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then why don't they fall down?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They are falling! The space station and everyone inside it are falling together, all the time.",
      "punch": "falling",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⬇️",
        "text": "Always falling!",
        "cue": "falling",
        "sub": "All together",
        "sub_cue": "together"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Falling? But they never hit the ground!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That's because the station zooms sideways super fast. As it falls, Earth curves away below it, so it keeps missing!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Falling around Earth",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🚀",
            "label": "Zooms sideways fast",
            "cue": "sideways"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "label": "Falls toward Earth",
            "cue": "falls"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌍",
            "label": "Earth curves away",
            "cue": "curves"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔄",
            "label": "Keeps missing!",
            "cue": "missing"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So they go round and round Earth?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Going round and round like that is called being in orbit.",
      "board": {
        "type": "orbit",
        "title": "In orbit",
        "center": "🌍",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🛰️",
            "label": "Station",
            "cue": "round"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "And because everything falls together, nothing presses down on the floor. So astronauts, their food and even water drops float around!",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Things that float",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🚀",
            "label": "Astronauts",
            "cue": "astronauts"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🥪",
            "label": "Food",
            "cue": "food"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "label": "Water drops",
            "cue": "water"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "It's like when a roller coaster drops and my tummy feels floaty!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! That floaty feeling is a tiny taste of what astronauts feel all day long.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎢",
